| `make secrets-install` `[read]` | Installs the secret scanner with no Go toolchain and no build, through `scripts/install_scanner.py`: it fetches the release archive config/project.json `secrets.scanner.release_assets` pins for this platform from `secrets.scanner.release_url`, installs its program under the per-user `secrets.scanner.install_root` only when the archive's sha256 is the pinned one, keeps the archive beside the program, and records the program's path, rev and sha256, so every scan, the commit hook's included, runs that program and no other. A second run fetches nothing and rewrites nothing only when the kept archive's sha256 is the pinned one and the program is its member, byte for byte; otherwise it installs again. | `make secrets-install` | [`secrets.scanner.release_url`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`secrets.scanner.release_assets.<platform>.sha256`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`secrets.scanner.install_root`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`secrets.scanner.rev`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`secrets.scanner.record_file`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`PY`](settings.md#make-variables) | Reads the network once per machine and pin, and writes outside the tree, under the install root; the record it writes in the tree is git-ignored. A name other than the adapted scanner's, an unlisted platform, an install root or program path inside the checkout and a record git would track are exit 14 before any fetch; an unreadable URL is exit 11; a local file it cannot read or write is exit 2 naming it; a sha256 that differs, a reply over `secrets.scanner.download_max_bytes` or an archive without exactly one program is exit 1 and installs nothing. Fetches `.tar.gz` archives only, so no Windows asset. Not a mirror: `secrets.scanner.release_url` names one. Not for scanning: `scripts/scan_secrets.py --staged` and `--history` do. A program or kept archive escaping install_root, or a record escaping the project, is exit 14 before any fetch or mutation. Checks judge paths at call time; a link swapped before the write is not caught. | [deterministic-checks.md](../guides/deterministic-checks.md) | always |
